# ============================================================
#  Expansion — short arcs for Professor Thorne, Old Maud and
#  Headmistress Marrow. All `trigger: social` (need met + rel).
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Professor Thorne ----------------

@event thorne_old_rival
title: An Old Rival
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 15 and year >= 2
weight: 12
art: duel
tags: rival study
scene: Two elderly mages facing each other across a dueling ring at dusk, one stern and grey, one flamboyant in purple, a nervous student holding a towel at the side.
text: A flamboyant old wizard in purple has arrived to settle "a forty-year-old matter" with Professor Thorne. A formal duel needs a second. Thorne looks around the courtyard and, to everyone's astonishment, points at you.
> left: Stand as his second
  rel thorne +10
  renown +4
  arcana +1
  say: The duel lasts four seconds. Thorne wins. Then both old men sit on the grass and laugh until they wheeze. You've never seen him laugh. Neither has anyone else.
> right: Politely decline
  rel thorne -3
  say: "Hm," says Thorne, and asks the caretaker instead. He wins anyway. He does not mention it again, which is somehow worse.

@event thorne_roses
title: The Professor's Roses
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 10 and month >= 7 and month <= 10
weight: 10
art: flower
tags: nature
scene: A severe old professor kneeling in a hidden rose garden at dawn, sleeves rolled up, murmuring encouragement to a single struggling rosebush.
text: At dawn, behind the observatory, you find Professor Thorne on his knees in a tiny walled rose garden, murmuring encouragement to a sickly bush. He sees you. Neither of you breathes.
> left: Back away and never speak of it
  rel thorne +6
  say: You leave. The next day in class he calls on you for the hardest question — and then, very quietly, gives you full marks for a so-so answer.
> right: Offer to help with the sick bush
  check alchemy 16:
    rel thorne +12
    alchemy +2
    say: You know the blight; Maud taught you. Within a month the bush is covered in red roses. Thorne leaves one, without comment, on your desk.
  else:
    rel thorne +4
    say: Your remedy does nothing. But Thorne lets you kneel beside him for an hour, saying nothing, which you suspect is a great honour.

@event thorne_shaking_hands
title: Thorne's Hands
trigger: social
actor: thorne
when: rel(thorne) >= 25 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: hand
tags: social
scene: An old professor gripping the edge of a lectern with both hands, a dropped wand on the floor, a single student in the doorway.
text: After class you see Thorne's wand slip from fingers that won't stop trembling. He picks it up, slowly. "Age," he says, not looking at you. "It comes for every storm eventually. You'll say nothing."
> left: Say nothing, as he asks
  rel thorne +8
  say: You never mention it. But you start arriving early to set up his demonstrations. He notices. He lets you.
> right: Tell Sister Amaranth
  rel thorne -6
  rel isolde +3
  say: Amaranth's tonic steadies his hands. Thorne is furious with you for a week. Then he stops being furious, and starts, grudgingly, teaching you his hardest spells — "before I can't."

# ---------------- Old Maud ----------------

@event maud_goat
title: Bartholomew in the Library
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 5
weight: 12
art: book
tags: nature
scene: A shaggy goat standing on a library table chewing a book, an apoplectic librarian below, an old woman in a straw hat hurrying through the stacks.
text: Maud's goat, Bartholomew, has got into the library and is eating the Restricted Section. The librarian is apoplectic. Maud, hurrying in, grabs your arm. "He likes you. Get him out before he eats anything with teeth."
> left: Lure him out with an apple
  check charm 12:
    rel maud +8
    say: Bartholomew follows the apple, and you, out into the sunlight. He has eaten one-third of "Curses of the Northern Wastes". He seems fine. Mostly.
  else:
    rel maud +4
    health -3
    say: Bartholomew eats the apple, then your sleeve, then headbutts you into a shelf. Maud gets him out in the end, laughing.
> right: Pick him up and carry him out
  vigor +2
  rel maud +6
  say: He is heavier than he looks and struggles like a sack of angry cats. You carry him all the way to the paddock. The librarian applauds.

@event maud_recipe
title: Maud's Soup
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 20
weight: 10
art: cauldron
tags: nature home
scene: A small cottage kitchen, a black iron pot over the fire, an old woman guiding a student's hand as they stir.
text: "I'm going to teach you my soup," says Maud, rolling up her sleeves. "Cures colds, broken hearts and most curses. Don't write it down. You'll remember it if you need it."
> left: Learn it properly
  alchemy +3
  rel maud +6
  say: It takes all afternoon. Some of the ingredients are herbs; some, as far as you can tell, are just stories. You remember every step.
> right: Mostly eat it
  health +8
  mood +5
  rel maud +3
  say: You learn about half of it and eat three bowls. Maud declares that the most important part of the recipe anyway.

@event maud_old_wand
title: A Wand From Sixty Years Ago
trigger: social
actor: maud
when: rel(maud) >= 30 and flag(knows_founders_seal)
weight: 14
art: wand
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: An old woman unwrapping a slender silver wand from a faded silk scarf, a photograph of three young students on the table beside it.
text: Maud unwraps something from a faded scarf: a slender silver wand. "Edmund's," she says. "He was the one who didn't come back. He'd have wanted it to go beneath the lake again, with someone who meant to close the door."
> left: Accept it
  arcana +3
  hollow +1
  flag edmunds_wand
  rel maud +8
  say: It fits your hand like it was waiting. When you hold it near the lake, it hums the same note as the drowned bell.
> right: Tell her to keep it
  rel maud +10
  mood +4
  say: "Keep it for him," you say. She holds it for a long time. "Sixty years," she says, "and nobody ever said that." She makes tea, and you sit with her until dark.

# ---------------- Headmistress Marrow ----------------

@event isolde_chess
title: A Game of Tower Chess
trigger: social
actor: isolde
when: rel(isolde) >= 10
weight: 10
art: crown
tags: study
scene: A chessboard of carved crystal towers on a small table by a tower window, two players, one candle, the lake silver below.
text: The headmistress keeps a board of crystal towers by her window. "Do you play?" she asks. It is clearly not a question. The pieces are already moving into position by themselves.
> left: Play to win (Lore)
  check lore 24:
    rel isolde +8
    lore +2
    say: You win. She looks at the board for a long moment, then laughs — a short, delighted sound. "Again," she says. "Thursday."
  else:
    rel isolde +4
    lore +1
    say: She wins in nine moves and spends the next hour showing you exactly why. It is the most useful lesson you've had all year.
> right: Play to learn how she thinks
  rel isolde +6
  guile +2
  say: You lose, slowly, watching. She sacrifices pieces she seems to love. By the end, you understand a great deal about how the academy is run.

@event isolde_portrait
title: The Young Headmistress
trigger: social
actor: isolde
when: rel(isolde) >= 5
weight: 8
art: mirror
tags: mystery
scene: A portrait in a forgotten corridor of a laughing young woman in student robes with a wand behind her ear, frame dusty, eyes unmistakably the headmistress's.
text: In a forgotten corridor you find a portrait of a laughing girl with a wand stuck behind her ear and ink on her nose. The plaque has been scratched off. The eyes are unmistakably the headmistress's. The portrait winks.
> left: Ask the portrait about her
  guile +1
  lore +1
  say: "Detention record of the decade," whispers the portrait. "Set the observatory on fire twice. Best student this castle ever had." It winks again.
> right: Tell the headmistress you found it
  rel isolde +6
  say: She is quiet for a moment. "I thought they'd burned it." She almost smiles. "Leave it where it is. Someone should remember her."

@event isolde_judgement
title: A Question of Mercy
trigger: social
actor: isolde
when: rel(isolde) >= 20 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: scales
tags: story
scene: The headmistress at her desk with a single file open, a student seated opposite, rain on the window behind them.
text: The headmistress slides a file across her desk. A second-year stole from the apothecary to pay for a sick mother's medicine. The rules say expulsion. "You're a student," she says. "Tell me what a student thinks is just."
> left: Argue for mercy
  rel isolde +6
  charm +1
  say: You argue for an hour. She listens to all of it. The second-year is given a job in the infirmary and a stern lecture. The mother recovers.
> right: The rules exist for a reason
  rel isolde +4
  lore +1
  say: "Yes," she says, "they do." She closes the file. You never learn what she decided, but the second-year is still in class the next week, looking grateful at nobody in particular.
